# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# JavaScript lockfiles. Deliberately untracked: this repo carried both an npm
# and a bun lockfile, and two of them cannot be kept honest at once. Installs
# resolve from package.json, so CI uses `npm install` rather than `npm ci`
# (which requires a lockfile), and actions/setup-node runs without its npm
# cache (which derives its key from one). Cargo.lock stays tracked: it has no
# rival, and it pins what actually goes into a shipped binary.
package-lock.json
bun.lock

# Frontend / desktop build artifacts
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
src-tauri/gen/
logs/
.DS_Store

# Default local documents used by the automation server
framework.document.json
framework.fw
.framework/
.framework-samples/

# Machine-local Codex server paths; keep the portable example.
.codex/config.toml

# Machine-local agent worktrees
.claude/worktrees/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Generated demo datasets (reproduce with: uv run examples/generate_accounting_demo.py)
demo-data*/
